# CQ 22: On which decomposition level is each resource assigned?
#
# Figure 5 shows one process at two levels of detail. A resource may be
# assigned on either, and assigning it on both counts the same work twice: the
# refined operators T11 and T12 do the work that T1 does in the coarse view,
# not work in addition to it.
#
# Test case 1 follows that rule and models T11 and T12 only. The question makes
# the rule checkable instead of leaving it in a comment: an answer naming one
# resource on an operator and on its parent is the double count.
#
# The level is the number of steps up to an operator that has no parent.
PREFIX vdi3682: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#>
SELECT ?resource ?operator (COUNT(?ancestor) AS ?level) ?parentAlsoAssigned
WHERE {
  ?operator vdi3682:hasAssignment ?assignment .
  ?assignment vdi3682:assignedResource ?resource .
  OPTIONAL { ?operator (^vdi3682:isComposedOf)+ ?ancestor }
  OPTIONAL {
    ?parent vdi3682:isComposedOf ?operator ; vdi3682:hasAssignment ?pa .
    ?pa vdi3682:assignedResource ?resource .
    BIND(?parent AS ?parentAlsoAssigned)
  }
} GROUP BY ?resource ?operator ?parentAlsoAssigned
  ORDER BY ?resource ?operator
